+/**
+ * What the bindings are asked for, and what a crossing costs (VitaSurf).
+ *
+ * The longest job on a GitHub load is 12388 ms and the five things
+ * counted so far come to 2910 of it, so nine and a half seconds are in
+ * bindings nobody counts. Every crossing that hands JavaScript a node
+ * goes through wrap_node, which looks the node up in a table of 128
+ * chains; a document of six thousand elements and seven thousand text
+ * nodes puts about a hundred entries in each. Count the calls, the
+ * hits, and the chain steps walked, so the average chain length is in
+ * the log rather than inferred.
